      "message": "d, new)` is true exactly for `('new','paid')`, `('new','cancelled')`, `('paid','refunded')`.\n- `CONTRACT_VERSION = 2` \u2014 copied constant, so downstream consumers can assert the pinned version.\n- `_ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS = frozenset({('new','paid'), ('new','cancelled'), ('paid','refunded')})` \u2014 the truth table copied verbatim into local code.\n- `can_transition(old, new)` \u2014 returns `(old, new) in _ALLOWED_TRANSITIONS`, matching the contract's membership-test behavior for arbitrary inputs (including non-string/`None` values, which simply fall through to `False`).\n- `consume(old, new)` \u2014 the requested downstream entry point; delegates to the local `can_transition`, so it preserves the v2 assumption rather than re-deriving or relaxing it.\n\nCheck coverage exercised: all three allowed transitions, self-transitions (`new\u2192new`), reverse/invalid pairs (`paid\u2192cancelled`, `refunded\u2192new`, `cancelled\u2192paid`), and `(None, None)`.\n\nNo other files were created or modified; no repository-wide tests were run."
